repro_steps: "${CMD:-npm} publish, npm $SUB, and { false; } && FLAG=--provenance each evade or corrupt publish auditing."
resolution: "Recognize braced parameter expansions, reject unresolved npm scalar subcommands, and preserve preceding command status across a standalone closing brace."
expected_result: Dynamic publish command/subcommand forms fail closed and closing braces preserve compound status.
actual_result: Narrow scalar matching and closing-brace status reset produce clean false passes.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T19:09:40.818Z",pi-agent,"All three findings reproduced. With scanner and verifier source reverted, dynamic publish failure counts were [0,0] instead of [1,1] and the brace-group assignment retained --provenance; SOURCE_ONLY_REVERT_EXIT=1. Restored source broadens parameter-expansion refusal, catches unresolved npm subcommands, and carries group status across the closing brace. npm test, 100% coverage, docstring, release:check, and real workflow attestation verification pass."
